  "goodToKnow": "Wahrlich means truly or indeed, and it sounds elevated or archaic. It's familiar from the Bible: Wahrlich, ich sage euch. Today, people use it for emphasis, often ironically: Das war wahrlich kein Meisterwerk. In everyday talk, wirklich, echt or tatsächlich are more normal. Also note wahrlich isn't an adjective: you can't say ein wahrlicher Freund (use wahrer Freund)."
